.TH KKTYPR 1 "November 2026" "kktypr 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kktypr \- A blazingly fast touch typing academy and developer syntax tutor for your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kktypr
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kktypr
is a high-performance terminal touch typing tutor and developer syntax trainer written in pure Rust (Edition 2024) powered by Ratatui and Crossterm.
It features stationary typewriter cursor layout physics, dual structured curricula (Fundamentals and Developer Code Syntax), real-time keystroke precision metrics, weak-key heatmap analysis, dynamic remedial drill synthesis, and a 60 FPS Word Drop arcade mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Return to previous menu or pause/exit active typing session.
.TP
\fBTab\fR / \fBShift-Tab\fR
Switch active view tabs or toggle options.
.TP
\fBArrow Keys\fR / \fBh, j, k, l\fR
Navigate menus, lessons, and profile entries.
.TP
\fBEnter\fR / \fBSpace\fR
Select lesson, confirm action, or restart drill.
.TP
\fBCtrl-c\fR
Safely exit application and restore terminal raw mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/kktypr/stats.json\fR
Atomic XDG state persistence containing user accuracy heatmaps, bigram error profiles, and lesson completion history.
